-- title:
--   Index of Γ∩ sΓ s⁻¹ equals the Hecke arrow degree
-- statement:
--   Write $H=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ for the quaternion algebra attached to rationals $a_1,b_1$ and $\hat H=H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ for its finite-adelic algebra, and $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a_1x_I^2-b_1x_J^2+a_1b_1x_K^2$. Let $N$ be a nonzero squarefree natural number and $q,q'$ primes with $q'\neq q$, $q,q'\ge 5$, neither dividing $N$. Assume $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and that for a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ the algebra $H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra precisely when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal $\mathbb Z$-order of $H$ and $R_1\le\Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection of two maximal orders whose additive relative index in the first is $N$. Let $n_1\in\hat H^\times$ lie in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $q$: $n_1$ and $q\,n_1^{-1}$ lie in the adelic box of $R_1$, while $n_1^{-1}$ and $q^{-1}n_1$ do not; assume the meet order $O=R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nq$. Let $v_2$ be a finite place containing $q$, let $\ell$ be a prime distinct from $q$ and $q'$, and let $s\in H^\times$, $s_f\in\hat H^\times$ satisfy: the component of $s_f$ is $s\otimes 1$ at every place not containing $q$ and $1$ at places containing $q$; the product of the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ with $s_f^{-1}$ lies in the prime Hecke set of $O$ at $\ell$ if $\ell\nmid N$, and, if $\ell\mid N$, in that set intersected with the conditions that conjugation by the element move $O$ and that $O$ not be contained in the corresponding conjugate of $\Lambda_1$; and $\mathrm{nrd}(s)=\ell$. Finally let $\Gamma\le H^\times$ consist exactly of the $x$ lying, at every finite place $w\neq v_2$, in the subgroup generated by the local unit box of $R_1$ at $w$, and with $\mathrm{ord}_q(\mathrm{nrd}(x))$ even. Then the relative index of $\Gamma\cap s\Gamma s^{-1}$ in $\Gamma$ equals $\ell$ if $\ell\mid N$ and $\ell+1$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the classical index computation $[\Gamma:\Gamma\cap s\Gamma s^{-1}]=\ell+1$ (resp. $\ell$ for $\ell\mid N$) for a quaternionic unit group of level $N$ and a global element $s$ of reduced norm $\ell$, here matched with the degree attached to the degeneracy arrow at $\ell$ in the Hecke tower. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik side comparison between the coset graph of the $q$-units and the adelic class sets, in particular in the identification of quotients and stabilisers for a Mumford-side frame.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraph_relIndex_inf_map_conj_eq_arrowDegree_of_hecke.lean

